.TH SYMLINKAT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
symlinkat \- create a directory-relative symbolic link
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "int symlinkat(const char* " target ", int " directory ", const char* " path ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a symbolic link at a path relative to the open directory descriptor,
or the current directory for
.BR AT_FDCWD .
An absolute link path ignores the descriptor. The target text is stored
unchanged, need not exist, and is not resolved against the descriptor.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success, leaving
.B errno
unchanged, or \-1 on failure with positive Linux
.BR errno .
.SH NOTES
Crunch errno is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR readlinkat (3crunch),
.BR symlinkat (2)
